---
// The record-diagram classes (.chip, .label, .small …) live in figures.css.
import "../styles/components/figures.css";
---

<figure class="standard-diagram">
  <svg
    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
    viewBox="0 0 960 356"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="rdr-conformance-title rdr-conformance-desc"
  >
    <title id="rdr-conformance-title">
      The four conformance levels as a ladder
    </title>
    <desc id="rdr-conformance-desc">
      Four ascending steps. Level 0 emitting, level 1 append-only, level 2
      dependent, and level 3 contestable. Each step names what it adds to the
      one below it.
    </desc>

    <text x="14" y="30" class="title ink"
      >Each rung adds one thing to the one below</text
    >
    <rect x="14" y="198" width="206" height="80" class="chip chip-state"></rect>
    <text x="117" y="223" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink"
      >Level 0 · Emitting</text
    >
    <text x="117" y="245" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >valid records, with as_of</text
    >
    <text x="117" y="262" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >kept apart from recorded_at</text
    >
    <line x1="220" y1="228" x2="240" y2="202" class="line dash"></line>

    <rect x="240" y="148" width="206" height="80" class="chip chip-state"
    ></rect>
    <text x="343" y="173" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink"
      >Level 1 · Append-only</text
    >
    <text x="343" y="195" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >nothing edited; every record</text
    >
    <text x="343" y="212" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >hashed and chained</text
    >
    <line x1="446" y1="178" x2="466" y2="152" class="line dash"></line>

    <rect x="466" y="98" width="246" height="80" class="chip chip-state"></rect>
    <text x="589" y="123" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink"
      >Level 2 · Dependent</text
    >
    <text x="589" y="145" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >depends_on and invalidated_by</text
    >
    <text x="589" y="162" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >populated; discrepancies answered</text
    >
    <line x1="712" y1="128" x2="732" y2="102" class="line dash"></line>

    <rect x="732" y="48" width="214" height="80" class="chip chip-state"></rect>
    <text x="839" y="73" text-anchor="middle" class="label ink"
      >Level 3 · Contestable</text
    >
    <text x="839" y="95" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >standing declared; objections</text
    >
    <text x="839" y="112" text-anchor="middle" class="small muted"
      >answered within a clock</text
    >

    <text x="14" y="308" class="small muted">
      A system declares the highest level every record it emits satisfies, and a
      consumer reads that as a floor
    </text>
    <text x="14" y="326" class="small muted">
      rather than a promise about any one record. Declaring Level 0 honestly is
      conformance.
    </text>
    <text x="14" y="344" class="small muted">
      Declaring Level 2 over a log that never populates invalidated_by is not.
    </text>
  </svg>
</figure>
